  "separator": {
    "why": "The Dream voice separator (src/wozmod/voices/separation.py). checkpoint: Kimberley Jensen's Mel-Band RoFormer vocal model (MIT), which packaging/separator_model.py makes the model files from. kernels: the two PTX builds of packaging/separator/kernels.cu that packaging/separator_kernels.py --cuda makes for the CUDA engine, each with the NVRTC compiler and the CUDA headers it is built with. That engine is out of every build (native/src/cuda.rs), so nothing here is used or shipped until it is turned back on. shaders: the glslang release that compiles packaging/separator/vulkan/ to SPIR-V for every other GPU, and how it is run (a build tool as well). Model files, PTX and SPIR-V are pinned in separation.MODEL, KERNELS and SHADERS. wheels: the pinned downloads those tools and the runtime come from (PyPI wheels, and glslang's release archive). files and licenses: what a release carries per system (packaging/separator_runtime.py): ONNX Runtime 1.32.0 for the CPU path. imports: on Windows, the wheel whose Visual C++ runtime files go beside a library that imports them; which files is read from the library's import table (packaging/windows_imports.py), not listed here.",
